!!! oculus/scene/manager-smoke.mat
!!! Smoke test for window management.
!!!
!!! Exercises: creating windows, focusing, raising, minimizing, and closing.

book oculus.scene.manager-smoke

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from oculus.window.geometry
read everything from oculus.window.lifecycle
read everything from oculus.window.operations
read everything from oculus.window.record
read everything from oculus.window.viewport
read everything from oculus.window.workspace
read everything from oculus.scene.manager

main returns number begin paragraph
    !!! Create a viewport with scaling.
    value vp is build viewport with physical-width being 1920, physical-height being 1080, logical-width being 1200, logical-height being 675, scale-x being 1.6, scale-y being 1.6
    
    !!! Create the scene manager.
    value sm is build scene-manager with revision being 0, viewport being vp, window-count being 0, max-windows being 64
    
    !!! Create the first window.
    value win-a is create-window with position-x being 10, position-y being 10, width being 800, height being 600, label being "Editor", window-id being 1
    
    !!! Verify window A geometry.
    when win-a.geometry.width is at least 800 then
        say "window A width correct"
    otherwise
        say "window A width failed"
    end when
    
    !!! Create a second window.
    value win-b is create-window with position-x being 820, position-y being 10, width being 370, height being 600, label being "Terminal", window-id being 2
    
    !!! Focus window A.
    value win-a-focused is focus-window with window-obj being win-a, should-focus being true
    when win-a-focused.focused is at least 1 then
        say "window A focused"
    otherwise
        say "window A focus failed"
    end when
    
    !!! Raise window B.
    value win-b-raised is raise-window with window-obj being win-b, new-z-index being 10
    when win-b-raised.z-index is at least 10 then
        say "window B raised"
    otherwise
        say "window B raise failed"
    end when
    
    !!! Minimize window A.
    value win-a-min is minimize-window with window-obj being win-a-focused
    
    !!! Verify window A is minimized using pattern matching.
    consider win-a-min.state
        when window-state.Minimized then
            say "window A minimized"
        otherwise
            say "window A minimize failed"
    end consider
    
    !!! Close window B.
    value win-b-closed is close-window with window-obj being win-b-raised
    
    !!! Verify window B is closed using pattern matching.
    consider win-b-closed.state
        when window-state.Closed then
            say "window B closed"
        otherwise
            say "window B close failed"
    end consider
    
    give 0
end paragraph
